          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Diluted household bleach and soap-based moss killers both kill moss within hours. Bleach mixed at about one part to four parts water is cheap and effective but browns nearby plants. Soap-based killers, made from potassium salts of fatty acids, act just as quickly and are gentler around greenery. Either works best on whatever is left after a dry scrape."
          }
