          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Used now and then, diluted and rinsed off well, bleach is unlikely to harm asphalt in any meaningful way, although some owners see slight lightening on pavement that is already faded. The bigger risk is to the lawn and plants beside the drive. Wet them and cover them before you start, and keep the runoff away from storm drains."
          }
        },
